WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
- I'm always looking for stories
that might make you smile.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.260
And we've got a great
one today, everybody.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.905
This is "What I'm Liking".

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.670
(upbeat music)
(crowd applauding)

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.400
An elementary school teacher
in Charlotte, North Carolina

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.170
is helping his students embrace

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.450
what he calls socially conscious art.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.540
Basically, he's influencing
them to observe the history

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.760
and current events that impact their lives

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.560
and interpret them creatively.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.050
We have this awesome educator
on the line right now

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.470
watching on Charlotte CW,
let's say hi to Jamil.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.303
What's up Jamil?

00:00:29.303 --> 00:00:31.318
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:31.318 --> 00:00:32.387
- Hello, hello.

00:00:32.387 --> 00:00:33.897
Thank you for having me on.

00:00:33.897 --> 00:00:35.790
- Hello. It's lovely to have you.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.250
And thank you first and
foremost for being an educator.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.200
We really love what you do.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.710
I think all parents really
appreciate it more now than ever

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.760
having to school our own kids
for a couple years there.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.860
But explain more about what you mean

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.280
by socially conscious art and
how do you teach it in class?

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.500
- Well, I believe that
socially conscious art

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.380
is thought provoking and
has a deeper meaning.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.870
And I like to teach that
way in my classroom.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.390
I recently just taught my
students about an artist

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:07.140
who I love by the name of
TJ Reddy who was an artist,

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.050
a poet and activist who spread
awareness through his art

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.670
about civil rights issues.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.710
And so, my fourth grade
students got the chance

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.440
to create self portraits in his style,

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.610
and I was so proud of them

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.920
because in the backgrounds
of their images,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:23.160
they incorporated things
about the war in Ukraine,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.220
about animal rights, about
the pandemic and homelessness.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.480
And I just really wanted them to know

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.280
that they could use their art as a way

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.290
to spread awareness about these issues.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.280
- Absolutely.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.290
God, that was powerful.
Just seeing those images.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:36.390
And also very therapeutic for them,

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.920
maybe if they have a hard
time talking about it,

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:38.940
to get it out like that.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.550
That's incredibly smart and clever.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:45.030
So, I hear that you're also a
working artist as well, right?

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:46.050
- I am. I am.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.760
I am a local muralist.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:50.190
I have several murals
around the Charlotte area

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:52.350
including one on permanent display

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.000
in Charlotte's Mint Museum.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.790
I'm currently working on 190-foot mural

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.620
in Charlotte's Historic West End

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.560
which is historically
African-American side of town.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.830
And I'm chronicling the
history of the corridor

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.470
by putting notable figures in the work

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.720
such as Dorothy Counts,
who was the first student

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.880
to integrate our schools
here in Charlotte.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.940
Julius Chambers who was
a prominent attorney

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.650
who helped to desegregate our schools.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.910
And Charles Jones who helped

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.250
to organize sit-ins in the 1960s.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.800
So, I like to use my
art as a teaching tool.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:23.730
- Wow.
- To show my students

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.430
that they, what I'm teaching in class,

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.380
I'm actually practicing in real life.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.670
And so my students got the
chance to come out to help me

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:36.090
spray paint flowers into the
background of my paintings.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.830
So, I was so excited about that.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:41.670
- What an amazing, immersive
way to teach kids about art,

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:44.280
but also educate them on
important historical figures

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.600
that we might not be talking about.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:46.890
That is so cool.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.390
Thank you so much, Jamil.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.988
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:49.988 --> 00:02:51.113
(audience applauding)

00:02:51.113 --> 00:02:52.377
- [Jamil] Thank you so much.

00:02:52.377 --> 00:02:54.840
- And you are so talented.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:55.673
And that's not all.

00:02:55.673 --> 00:02:56.730
- Thank you.
- Our season long partner,

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.170
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.940
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show".

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.490
They wanna honor ultimate
overachievers just like you, sir.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.100
So, they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.242
How's that sound?

00:03:06.242 --> 00:03:07.565
(crowd cheering)
- Oh wow.

00:03:07.565 --> 00:03:08.398
(Kelly chuckling)

00:03:08.398 --> 00:03:09.499
Thank you.

00:03:09.499 --> 00:03:11.449
Thank you so much.
- Absolutely.

